            <ArticleTitle>[Thrombosis of the sigmoid sinus and transverse sinus with an unusual course].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>71-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of intracranial complication in patient with cephalgia and short period of the temperature without signs of sharpening chronic otitis is reported. At the time of the operation epidural abscess of fossa cranial posterior, perisinusal abscess and thrombus of sigmoid sinus, abscess in transverse sinus were found.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
